@AppleSupport How do I set my Macbook Pro's resolution to 1280x720 without attaching a 2nd monitor? 13" Mid 2014 with Sierra @275675 Try setting that by following this article: https://t.co/jurYWmUNKR

Let us know if this helps. @AppleSupport I have read a couple of these kinds of articles, but I want this to work without having to attach a second monitor. I just want to set the resolution and then record my screen. And then upload to Youtube. @275675 Check these steps out from the article: 
Set the resolution for the primary display: Choose Apple menu &gt; System Preferences, click Displays, then click Display. Pick Scaled, then select one of the options. After Scaled, you should see the resolution you want.

